[Music]  welcome back to another episode of the  heroes path  a series in which we follow the journeys  the different heroes  champions and other key figures  underwent during the rise of ganon  otherwise known as the great calamity if  you haven't seen any of the previous  parts  this video might confuse you as it skips  any introduction and jumps right into  the story events taking place at the  moment the disaster starts  in that case i advise you to watch the  episode about link and zelda first  as that one gives a more thorough  introduction to the series and  its purpose joining me today is breath  of the wild scientist croton  who is best known for his amazing videos  about the stats  analysis and the inner workings of the  game if you are unfamiliar with his  channel  i highly recommend giving his content a  watch links to his  channel and one of his videos will be in  the description and the end card as per  tradition in this series  with that said let's get back to  business  the champions gather around zelda as she  returns from the spring of wisdom  having failed to awaken their ceiling  power yet again the champion shares some  comforting wards  and mifa tries to give the desperate  princess advice on finding the spark she  needs to unlock her sacred gift  however as fate would have it before she  is able to finish her last sentence  a huge tremor interrupts her and sends  her and the rest of the party in a state  of disarray  calamity ganon has finally decided to  show his face  and today of all days with some quick  coordination  the plan is clear link and zelda will  make their way to hyrule castle  while the pilots make haste for their  divine beasts to provide support to the  hero  and princess in their fight against the  demon king with the exception of rivali  the group moves along the stone-carved  roads of the linero promenade  at the west gate they take a left turn  into the canyon leading towards  cockregal village  the hometown of the chica tribe however  mifa never crosses to the village  herself  as link zelda and urbosa continue on  towards kakariko  mifa joins druk and moves over a quarter  shelf  after which the two scaled the cliffside  down into the lanero wetlands  gopanga village was a fairly large  settlement located in the wetlands  although creating a champion does not  depict mifa visiting the settlements  age of calamity might choose to alter  this scenario and we will see mifa  joined rook in fending off a possible  monster invasion in gopanga  this means that we might get to choose  between one of the two characters  in this mission providing the player the  option to play as the champion of choice  beyond this point mifa's journey will  mostly consist of traversing through the  water  so this would be a good solution to give  her some grounded combat sections during  the calamity  rather than before it although creating  a champion depicts their paths mostly  without detours  the champions wouldn't be careless about  innocent civilians in dire need of their  assistance  the book is a great piece of lore and  presents a good overview of the  estimated paths our heroes traversed  but at the end of the day it is just  that an estimation  diverting from these guidelines slightly  is not a crime if it complements the  gameplay and the story progression of  the characters  from the wetlands mifa moves east into  the rotella river and up around kinzian  island  she then crosses in between the pier and  boney pond  and east into the zora river which leads  to her home  zora's domain if age of calamity wants  to stick to the core story events  established in breath of the wild  mifa should never encounter a single  guardian on her journey  not only is it far too early for any  guardians to have arrived this far from  the castle  but zora's domain nor its surrounding  rivers or lakes were ever reached by the  automata  similar to kakariko village the domain  is obscured from view and hidden away  from sight by a natural border of  mountains and cliffs  making it one of the safer places during  the calamity the closest dead guardian  we can find to the home of the zora  lies east of bonnet pond close to what  will later be the location of the la  neru tower in the era of the wild  this location is still a long ways away  from zora's domain  and most likely just a leftover of the  army that torched kaponga village or  more garrison to the west of the  wetlands  no other guardian husks are found beyond  this point  obviously the zora thrive inside a body  of water whereas their average land  speed is no different than the average  hylian or gerudo  in the waters they can reach far greater  speeds  hence it's no surprise that mifa's path  consists of more than 50 percent of  traversal through rivers  however the zora aren't the only beings  who thrive in an aquatic environment  the zora river as well as the roads  running alongside it are notorious for  housing large quantities of lithophos  and although lizofoes seem kind of  brainless in breath of the wild  some of the backstory of the game  sketches a whole different picture of  these speedy water monsters  as according to the zora stone monument  one of the zora kings of old along with  this army was ambushed by a battalion of  these creatures under the command of a  lizofo's general  this indicates a clear intelligence and  coordination between these beings  and since they are now under the  influence of ganon and more restless and  dangerous than ever before  seen they may provide a decent challenge  since they are pretty much at the same  advantage while submerged  a water-based battle up the zora river  between mifa and hordes of lisophos  would be a perfect  fit for the zora champion we might even  get to choose to either engage them on  land or in the water by skipping between  the river and the roads next to it  similar to the case of ravali it all  depends on if the team at cui tecmo is  able to integrate this kind of gameplay  into the warriors engine  if not they might just stick to land  combat although that would be a shame as  it is not logical for azor ah to choose  land over water  especially when they're in a hurry since  mifa's journey tour divine beast is by  far the shortest of all the champions  and doesn't cross many important  settlements or locations  we will once again present an  alternative option to the one presented  in creating a champion  since according to the book once mifa  reaches the oren bridge  she moves straight into the zodobon  highlands and subsequently  up this unnamed peak which is allegedly  the standby position of varuta  however it is hard to imagine mifa going  straight to her divine beast without  checking up on zorro's domain first  despite the fact that her home was  spared the destruction by guardians  that isn't to say that it wasn't under  attack at all  as mentioned before the zelfels are  bountiful in this region  and historically the providence is even  notorious for being plagued by lionels  who reside in the surrounding mountains  mifa has plenty of reasons to chuck up  on her people but the one that stands  out the most  the safety of her brother saidan who was  just a young child  at this time and who mifa has a strong  sense of responsibility for  with this scenario in mind instead of  going straight to varuta  she continues up zoro river past ruto  lake and  into her hometown a battle at zoro's  domain between mifa the zora soldiers  and her father king dorafin and hordes  of incoming monsters would be a great  setting for some amazing action  sequences  where the zora must defend the great  zoro bridge to deny  access to any monster bold enough to try  to cross into their territory  not only that but this would also  present the option for us  the player to take control of another  character if we so choose  we are of course talking about king  doraphan himself  the king of the zora has been depicted  as a brave and battle-hardened warrior  himself in the backstory of breath of  the wild  when we stated before that no guardian  ever touched store's domain  this is actually not entirely true  though it didn't actually do any damage  to the home of the zora  one stray guardian did manage to get  dangerously close to the domain  in upland's arena the scar on dorothea's  head  is said to have been a remnant of his  heroic action to take down this guardian  some have speculated that this might be  the same guardian we found at bonee pons  however this does not exactly match the  story told on the zora monuments  as it is quite far away from zoro's  domain itself  whatever the case may be the fight  between dorafan  and the stray machine may actually be a  gameplay section  and solely playable as him as soon as  the situation at zora's domain is under  control  mifa finally makes her way to varuta and  readies herself and the divine beast for  an attack on the source of all the chaos  the demon king himself who still resides  at hyrule castle  but in a turn of events ganon releases  more strands of malice aimed straight at  the colossal machine  and seizing control of it with mifa now  trapped inside her corrupted weapon  a ghostly specter manifests itself  before her  eyes a being whose sole purpose is to  prevent anyone from retaking the machine  and kill the pilot within armed with her  light skill trident she desperately  tries to get the upper hand on water  blight ganon  but as we all know it isn't meant to be  mifa is slain by the demon king's  creation and just like her fellow pilots  her spirit will linger within varuta for  the next 100 years to come  unable to escape the walls of the  machine she was so proud to be chosen to  pilot  the death of the zora champion inflicted  a huge grief on her people  and zora's domain as a whole fell into a  deep misery in the days after zelda  sacrificed herself to seal away calamity  ganon and the flames of war  slowly extinguished the zora people  planned to send mifa's trident drifting  down zora river as a way to repose her  soul  however this act of remorse is  interrupted by mifa's voice who says  that the trident and her are one  and urges her fellow zora not to grieve  over her loss  but rather to remember it since that  moment her trident is kept safe  and cherished and a statue in her honor  is built  which to this day decorates the central  square of the domain  the zora have by far the longest  lifespan of hyrule's races  most of the zora elders present in the  era of the wild 100 years later were  alive during the rise of calamity ganon  and the zora princess still remains a  sensitive subject among her people  for her brother saidon who is now an  energetic adult and accomplished sora  warrior  the memory of the great calamity is but  a hazy dream  but due to the combined effort of him  and link during the era of the wild  mifa will be granted a chance for  revenge on ganon  not just for herself but also her people  [Music]  you

